Description: Do not read past the end of a short AppStream category
 The home page builds nine category rows with "for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++)"
 over the list of applications AppStream returned for that category. A Debian
 system's categories routinely contain fewer than ten desktop applications, and
 items[i] then reads past the end of the QList: the store segfaults while its
 main window is being constructed, before it can draw anything.
 .
 Debian 1.2.5-2.1 fixes this by porting to Qt 6 and changing the loop to
 qMin(10, items.size()). This patch applies only that one-line bound (plus the
 comment) to the Qt 5 source, so no unrelated component changes.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ubuntudde/dde-store/pull/34
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1117833
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
--- a/pages/homepage.cpp
+++ b/pages/homepage.cpp
@@ -65,7 +65,12 @@
             for (App *app : map.values()) {
                 items.insert(0, app);
             }
-            for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
+            // An AppStream category on a normal Debian system usually has
+            // fewer than ten desktop applications. Reading items[i] past the
+            // end is undefined behaviour and crashed the store while it was
+            // building this page - the segfault seen on the Chromebook.
+            // Fixed upstream in 1.2.5-2.1 (Debian #1112833).
+            for (int i = 0; i < qMin(10, items.size()); i++) {
                 list->addItem(items[i]->name, items[i]->icon, i);
                 apps->append(items[i]);
             }
